cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use BeastXPy in your work, please cite it using this metadata. A DOI
  will be added to this record once the release has been archived.
title: "BeastXPy: a reproducible Python workflow for BEAST 1 divergence-time inference"
abstract: >-
  BeastXPy turns a strict YAML description into BEAST 1 / BEAST X XML,
  validates it through four gates, runs a seed matrix, and reports MCMC
  diagnostics, marginal-likelihood comparisons and reproducibility artefacts.
  It is an independent workflow layer, not a reimplementation of BEAST. The
  Python code is MIT-licensed; the bundled unmodified BEAST jars are
  LGPL-2.1-only (see NOTICE).
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-22"
license: "MIT AND LGPL-2.1-only"
keywords:
  - phylogenetics
  - BEAST
  - divergence time
  - MCMC
  - reproducibility
  - Bayesian inference
